{"severity":"error","file":"errors/pure_violation_2.march","start_line":17,"start_col":2,"end_line":17,"end_col":17,"message":"`mod LeakyPure` (declared `cap pure`) declares `needs IO.Random`, but a pure module cannot hold a capability: `needs` exists only to admit side effects, directly or through a stdlib wrapper such as `File.read` or `DateTime.now`.\n\nRemove the `needs` line, and move the code that needs it to a module without `cap pure`.","code":"pure_violation","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CONTRACT"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/pure_violation_2.march","start_line":21,"start_col":4,"end_line":21,"end_col":16,"message":"`gen` in `mod LeakyPure` (declared `cap pure`) calls `random_bytes`, which has side effects.\n\nUse pure functions (no IO, spawn, vault, clock, or random ops) in a `cap pure` module.","code":"pure_violation","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CONTRACT"}
